# The LWS test vocabulary: every lwst: class, property and individual used by the
# definitions, with its meaning. EXECUTION.md is the operational contract; this is the
# RDF view of the same terms, and the document the lwst: namespace should serve.
"@context":
  rdf: http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#
  rdfs: http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#
  owl: http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#
  xsd: http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#
  dcterms: http://purl.org/dc/terms/
  mf: http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#
  lwst: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1#
  id: "@id"
  type: "@type"
  label: rdfs:label
  comment: rdfs:comment
  subClassOf: {"@id": rdfs:subClassOf, "@type": "@id"}
  domain: {"@id": rdfs:domain, "@type": "@id"}
  range: {"@id": rdfs:range, "@type": "@id"}
  isDefinedBy: {"@id": rdfs:isDefinedBy, "@type": "@id"}
"@graph":
  - id: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
    type: owl:Ontology
    label: LWS test vocabulary
    comment: >-
      Terms for declarative conformance tests of the Linked Web Storage Protocol 1.0 and its
      authentication suites. Test manifests use the W3C test-manifest vocabulary (mf:) for
      manifests and entries and the RDF test vocabulary (rdft:) for approval status. The
      namespace is the one lws-test-suite uses; it is not yet published by W3C.
  - id: lwst:ValidationTest
    type: rdfs:Class
    subClassOf: mf:ManifestEntry
    label: "Validation test"
    comment: >-
      A test whose steps exercise behaviour the specification requires and assert the
      responses a conforming server gives.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:NegativeTest
    type: rdfs:Class
    subClassOf: mf:ManifestEntry
    label: "Negative test"
    comment: >-
      A test whose point is a refusal: at least one step expects a 4xx response, and the
      test also checks that the refused request had no effect.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Step
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Step"
    comment: >-
      One HTTP exchange of a test: a request, the expectations on its response, and the
      variables it captures. Steps run in order; a test fails at its first failing step.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Request
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Request"
    comment: >-
      What the harness sends in a step.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Response expectation"
    comment: >-
      What the harness checks in the response to a step's request. Every expectation
      present must hold.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:LinkExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Link expectation"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the Link header field (RFC 8288) of a response, or a Link value to
      send in a request.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:HeaderExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Header expectation"
    comment: >-
      A condition on one header field of a response, or a header to send in a request.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Challenge expectation"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the WWW-Authenticate header field, parsed into challenges per RFC
      9110 section 11.6.1.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ParameterExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Parameter expectation"
    comment: >-
      A condition on one auth-param of a challenge. Parameter names compare case-
      insensitively.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:JsonExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "JSON expectation"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the value a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) selects in a JSON response body,
      a JWT header or a JWT claims set.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:JwtExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "JWT expectation"
    comment: >-
      Conditions on a JWT captured earlier: its signature verifies against a JWKS and its
      header and claims satisfy JSON expectations.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:LocationExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Location expectation"
    comment: >-
      The response carries a Location header; its value, resolved against the request URL,
      is captured.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Prerequisites
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Prerequisites"
    comment: >-
      The state a test needs before its first step: resources the engine creates, as
      alice, and the access it grants on them. A failure to establish it is setup, not a
      finding: the outcome is cantTell, or inapplicable for access the target cannot
      grant.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Prerequisite resource"
    comment: >-
      A container or data resource the engine creates inside ${test.container}, or inside
      an earlier entry, before the test runs. The server chooses its URI; the entry's
      container or dataResource names the variable bound to it.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Resource authorization"
    comment: >-
      Access the engine grants on a prerequisite resource through the storage's access
      grant service, by LWS action. alice, who creates the resource, needs no grant.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ConnegExpectation
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Content-negotiation expectation"
    comment: >-
      Refetching the same URL once per listed media type yields responses with byte-
      identical bodies whose Content-Type echoes the type requested.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:IdentityRegistry
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Identity registry"
    comment: >-
      The document listing every identity tests may name.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Identity
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Identity"
    comment: >-
      An abstract agent and the credential the harness produces for it. Tests name
      identities, never credentials.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Level
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Requirement level"
    comment: >-
      The BCP 14 strength of what a test asserts. A test has exactly one level.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Trait
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Trait"
    comment: >-
      A facet of what a test exercises, used to select and group tests.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Capability
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Capability"
    comment: >-
      Something the harness or the target deployment must provide that the server under
      test cannot reveal about itself. A test requiring a capability the target lacks is
      inapplicable.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:IdentityKind
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Identity kind"
    comment: >-
      How an identity's credential is used.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Fault
    type: rdfs:Class
    label: "Credential fault"
    comment: >-
      The single defect that distinguishes a fault identity from its basis identity.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MUST
    type: lwst:Level
    label: "MUST"
    comment: >-
      Failing the test means the server does not conform.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:SHOULD
    type: lwst:Level
    label: "SHOULD"
    comment: >-
      Failing the test is reported as advisory; it does not decide conformance.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MAY
    type: lwst:Level
    label: "MAY"
    comment: >-
      An optional behaviour; failing the test is reported as advisory.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Get
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "GET"
    comment: >-
      Uses the GET method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Head
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "HEAD"
    comment: >-
      Uses the HEAD method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Post
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "POST"
    comment: >-
      Uses the POST method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Put
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "PUT"
    comment: >-
      Uses the PUT method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Patch
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "PATCH"
    comment: >-
      Uses the PATCH method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Delete
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "DELETE"
    comment: >-
      Uses the DELETE method.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Container
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Container"
    comment: >-
      Exercises containers.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:DataResource
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Data resource"
    comment: >-
      Exercises data resources.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Linkset
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Linkset"
    comment: >-
      Exercises linkset resources.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:StorageDescription
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Storage description"
    comment: >-
      Exercises the storage description resource.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Discovery
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Discovery"
    comment: >-
      Exercises discovery through links, challenges or metadata.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Authn
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Authentication"
    comment: >-
      Exercises authentication.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Authz
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Authorization"
    comment: >-
      Exercises authorization decisions.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Public
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Public"
    comment: >-
      Exercises resources readable without credentials.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Private
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Private"
    comment: >-
      Exercises resources that require credentials.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Conditional
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Conditional requests"
    comment: >-
      Exercises entity tags and preconditions.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Conneg
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Content negotiation"
    comment: >-
      Exercises content negotiation.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Range
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Range requests"
    comment: >-
      Exercises byte-range requests.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:TokenExchange
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Token exchange"
    comment: >-
      Exercises the authorization server's RFC 8693 token exchange.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:AccessGrants
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Access requests and grants"
    comment: >-
      Exercises access requests and grants.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Notifications
    type: lwst:Trait
    label: "Notifications"
    comment: >-
      Exercises notifications.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Authentication
    type: lwst:Capability
    label: "Authentication enforced"
    comment: >-
      The target storage enforces authentication on the run root: an anonymous request is
      challenged, and alice and bob are distinct authenticated agents.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:HarnessIssuedTokens
    type: lwst:Capability
    label: "Harness-issued access tokens"
    comment: >-
      The storage trusts an authorization server whose signing key the harness holds, so
      the harness can mint otherwise-valid access tokens with one chosen defect.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ReachableFixtures
    type: lwst:Capability
    label: "Reachable fixtures"
    comment: >-
      The target can reach the harness fixture host at ${fixtures.baseUrl} (identity
      documents, OpenID Provider, JWKS).
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:SamlTrust
    type: lwst:Capability
    label: "SAML trust"
    comment: >-
      The target's authorization server trusts the harness SAML identity provider's
      signing certificate.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:NoCredential
    type: lwst:IdentityKind
    label: "No credential"
    comment: >-
      Requests carry no Authorization header.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:StorageAccessToken
    type: lwst:IdentityKind
    label: "Storage access token"
    comment: >-
      Requests made as this identity carry Authorization: Bearer with an access token for
      the storage.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:SubjectCredential
    type: lwst:IdentityKind
    label: "Subject credential"
    comment: >-
      The identity's credential is a subject_token presented at the token endpoint; it is
      never sent as a storage access token.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:SignatureCorrupted
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Signature corrupted"
    comment: >-
      The signature no longer verifies: the last byte of a JWS signature is flipped, or a
      signed SAML element is altered after signing. Header and claims are unchanged.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:AlgNone
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Unsigned (alg none)"
    comment: >-
      The JWS header alg is "none" and the signature part is empty. Claims are unchanged.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:UnknownKeyId
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Unknown key"
    comment: >-
      Signed by a key the verifier cannot find: a fresh key whose kid is "touchstone-
      unknown-kid", which appears in no published JWKS or controlled identifier document.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Expired
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Expired"
    comment: >-
      iat is now minus 3900 s and exp is now minus 3600 s (SAML: NotOnOrAfter an hour
      past); validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:NotYetValid
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Not yet valid"
    comment: >-
      nbf is now plus 3600 s; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:IssuedInFuture
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Issued in the future"
    comment: >-
      iat is now plus 3600 s and exp now plus 3900 s; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:WrongAudience
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Wrong audience"
    comment: >-
      aud is ["https://not-this-storage.invalid/"]; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MultipleAudiences
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Multiple audiences"
    comment: >-
      aud is [the storage realm, "https://another-storage.invalid/"]; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:WrongIssuer
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Wrong issuer"
    comment: >-
      iss is "https://untrusted-issuer.invalid/"; signed by the key the storage trusts.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:AudienceExcludesAuthorizationServer
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Audience excludes the authorization server"
    comment: >-
      aud is ["https://not-the-authorization-server.invalid/"]; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ClientIdMismatch
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "client_id mismatch"
    comment: >-
      client_id is "https://other-client.invalid/" while sub and iss are unchanged;
      validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MissingExpiration
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Missing exp"
    comment: >-
      The exp claim is removed; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MissingIssuedAt
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Missing iat"
    comment: >-
      The iat claim is removed; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:MissingAuthorizedParty
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Missing azp"
    comment: >-
      The azp claim is removed; validly signed.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:UntrustedIssuer
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Untrusted OpenID Provider"
    comment: >-
      Issued and validly signed by a second harness OpenID Provider at
      ${fixtures.baseUrl}rogue-op, which publishes discovery and JWKS but is not named in
      the subject's controlled identifier document.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:Unsigned
    type: lwst:Fault
    label: "Unsigned assertion"
    comment: >-
      The SAML assertion carries no ds:Signature.
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:specification
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "specification"
    comment: >-
      A dated specification snapshot the manifest's tests were checked against.
    domain: mf:Manifest
    range: rdfs:Resource
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:identities
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "identities"
    comment: >-
      An identity in the registry.
    domain: lwst:IdentityRegistry
    range: lwst:Identity
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:level
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "level"
    comment: >-
      The test's requirement level.
    domain: mf:ManifestEntry
    range: lwst:Level
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:traits
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "traits"
    comment: >-
      A facet the test exercises.
    domain: mf:ManifestEntry
    range: lwst:Trait
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:requires
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "requires"
    comment: >-
      A capability the test (or identity) needs; absent on the target, the test is
      inapplicable.
    range: lwst:Capability
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:as
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "as"
    comment: >-
      Name of the identity whose credential authorizes the step's request (on a test, the
      default for its steps). Unset means alice.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:steps
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "steps"
    comment: >-
      The test's ordered steps.
    domain: mf:ManifestEntry
    range: lwst:Step
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:precondition
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "precondition"
    comment: >-
      When true, a failing expectation in this step makes the test inapplicable instead of
      failed, and no later step runs.
    domain: lwst:Step
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:request
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "request"
    comment: >-
      The request a step sends. Directly on a test, with response, it is shorthand for a
      test of exactly one step.
    range: lwst:Request
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:response
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "response"
    comment: >-
      The expectations on the step's response. Directly on a test, with request, it is
      shorthand for a test of exactly one step.
    range: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:prereqs
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "prereqs"
    comment: >-
      The state the test needs before its first step; the engine establishes it
      (EXECUTION.md section 4.3).
    domain: mf:ManifestEntry
    range: lwst:Prerequisites
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:hierarchy
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "hierarchy"
    comment: >-
      The resources to create, in order; an entry is created before any entry inside it.
    domain: lwst:Prerequisites
    range: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:container
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "container"
    comment: >-
      Creates a container and binds the variable this names to the URI the server assigns.
    domain: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:dataResource
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "dataResource"
    comment: >-
      Creates a data resource with the entry's content and binds the variable this names
      to the URI the server assigns.
    domain: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:in
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "in"
    comment: >-
      The variable of an earlier container entry to create this resource in. Unset means
      ${test.container}.
    domain: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:authorization
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "authorization"
    comment: >-
      Access to grant on the resource once it exists.
    domain: lwst:PrerequisiteResource
    range: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:read
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "read"
    comment: >-
      An identity granted the read action (GET, HEAD). anonymous means the public: the
      assignee is foaf:Agent.
    domain: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:modify
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "modify"
    comment: >-
      An identity granted the modify action (PUT, PATCH). anonymous means the public.
    domain: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:create
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "create"
    comment: >-
      An identity granted the create action (POST into a container). anonymous means the
      public.
    domain: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:delete
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "delete"
    comment: >-
      An identity granted the delete action (DELETE). anonymous means the public.
    domain: lwst:ResourceAuthorization
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:method
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "method"
    comment: >-
      The HTTP method, in upper case.
    domain: lwst:Request
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:url
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "url"
    comment: >-
      Template for the target URL; a relative reference is resolved against
      ${target.baseUrl}.
    domain: lwst:Request
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:contentType
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "contentType"
    comment: >-
      On a request, the Content-Type to send. On a response, the media type expected:
      type/subtype compared case-insensitively, parameters ignored.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:accept
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "accept"
    comment: >-
      The Accept header value to send.
    domain: lwst:Request
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:ifMatch
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "ifMatch"
    comment: >-
      If-Match value to send, a template; the literal current means HEAD the URL first, as
      the same identity, and send the ETag it returns (no If-Match if it returns none).
    domain: lwst:Request
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:linkHeaders
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "linkHeaders"
    comment: >-
      A Link value to send, or a condition on the response's Link values.
    range: lwst:LinkExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:rel
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "rel"
    comment: >-
      A link relation type: a registered name compared case-insensitively, or an extension
      relation URI compared exactly.
    domain: lwst:LinkExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:href
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "href"
    comment: >-
      Template for a link target, compared after resolving both sides against the request
      URL.
    domain: lwst:LinkExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:mediaType
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "mediaType"
    comment: >-
      The expected (or sent) type target attribute of a link.
    domain: lwst:LinkExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:otherHeaders
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "otherHeaders"
    comment: >-
      A header to send, or a condition on one response header.
    range: lwst:HeaderExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:headerName
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "headerName"
    comment: >-
      The header field name, compared case-insensitively.
    domain: lwst:HeaderExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:headerValue
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "headerValue"
    comment: >-
      Template for the value to send, or the exact expected value of some field line.
    domain: lwst:HeaderExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:differsFrom
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "differsFrom"
    comment: >-
      Template; the header must be present and no field line may equal this value.
    domain: lwst:HeaderExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:body
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "body"
    comment: >-
      Template for a body sent as UTF-8 text: a request's, or a prerequisite data
      resource's content.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:bodyURL
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "bodyURL"
    comment: >-
      A fixture file, relative to the definition document: the bytes to send, or the bytes
      the response body must equal exactly.
    range: rdfs:Resource
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:bodyJSON
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "bodyJSON"
    comment: >-
      A JSON value sent as a body (a request's, or a prerequisite data resource's
      content); string members are templates. Content-Type defaults to application/json.
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:bodyForm
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "bodyForm"
    comment: >-
      A JSON object of string templates sent as application/x-www-form-urlencoded; members
      appear in document order.
    domain: lwst:Request
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:statusCode
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "statusCode"
    comment: >-
      An acceptable status: an integer, or a class string such as "4xx". Several values
      mean any of them.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: rdfs:Literal
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:location
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "location"
    comment: >-
      The response must carry Location.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: lwst:LocationExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:authenticationChallenge
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "authenticationChallenge"
    comment: >-
      Some challenge in WWW-Authenticate must satisfy this expectation.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:wwwAuthenticate
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "wwwAuthenticate"
    comment: >-
      The challenge's auth-scheme, compared case-insensitively (lws-test-suite's term).
    domain: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:asUri
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "asUri"
    comment: >-
      The challenge's as_uri auth-param: a template it must equal exactly, or a parameter
      expectation (present, matches, capture).
    domain: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:realm
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "realm"
    comment: >-
      The challenge's realm auth-param: a template it must equal exactly, or a parameter
      expectation (present, matches, capture).
    domain: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:params
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "params"
    comment: >-
      A condition on one of the challenge's auth-params.
    domain: lwst:ChallengeExpectation
    range: lwst:ParameterExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:paramName
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "paramName"
    comment: >-
      The auth-param name.
    domain: lwst:ParameterExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:paramValue
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "paramValue"
    comment: >-
      Template for the exact expected auth-param value, after unquoting.
    domain: lwst:ParameterExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:bodyEmpty
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "bodyEmpty"
    comment: >-
      When true, the response has no content.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:bodyMatches
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "bodyMatches"
    comment: >-
      A regular expression (portable dialect) that must find a match in the body decoded
      as UTF-8.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:json
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "json"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the body parsed as JSON.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:pointer
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "pointer"
    comment: >-
      An RFC 6901 JSON Pointer; the empty pointer selects the whole value.
    domain: lwst:JsonExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:optional
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "optional"
    comment: >-
      When true, the expectation holds vacuously if the pointer selects nothing.
    domain: lwst:JsonExpectation
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:some
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "some"
    comment: >-
      The selected value is an array with at least one element satisfying every nested
      expectation (pointers relative to the element).
    domain: lwst:JsonExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:every
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "every"
    comment: >-
      The selected value is an array whose every element satisfies every nested
      expectation.
    domain: lwst:JsonExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:none
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "none"
    comment: >-
      The selected value is an array with no element satisfying all of the nested
      expectations.
    domain: lwst:JsonExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:jwt
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "jwt"
    comment: >-
      Conditions on a compact-serialized JWT.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: lwst:JwtExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:token
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "token"
    comment: >-
      Template yielding the JWT to check, usually a variable captured in the same step.
    domain: lwst:JwtExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:jwks
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "jwks"
    comment: >-
      Template yielding a JWKS URL; the JWT's signature must verify with the key its kid
      names there.
    domain: lwst:JwtExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:header
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "header"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the decoded JWT header.
    domain: lwst:JwtExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:claims
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "claims"
    comment: >-
      A condition on the decoded JWT claims set.
    domain: lwst:JwtExpectation
    range: lwst:JsonExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:connegEquivalent
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "connegEquivalent"
    comment: >-
      The step's URL serves one document under several media types.
    domain: lwst:ResponseExpectation
    range: lwst:ConnegExpectation
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:accepts
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "accepts"
    comment: >-
      The media types to request, in order.
    domain: lwst:ConnegExpectation
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:present
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "present"
    comment: >-
      When true, the header or auth-param is present; when false, it is absent.
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:absent
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "absent"
    comment: >-
      On a link expectation: no Link value satisfies its other conditions (a header's
      absence is present: false). On a prerequisite resource: the engine does not create
      it, and binds its variable to a fresh URI inside its parent that names nothing.
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:equals
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "equals"
    comment: >-
      The selected JSON value equals this one (deep equality; strings are templates).
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:equalsIri
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "equalsIri"
    comment: >-
      Template for an absolute IRI; the selected string, resolved against the request URL,
      equals it.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:matches
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "matches"
    comment: >-
      A regular expression in the portable dialect of EXECUTION.md (unanchored search; a
      leading (?i) makes it case-insensitive). On a header, some field line or the
      combined value matches; on JSON, a string value matches, any other value is matched
      as its compact JSON text.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:hasValue
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "hasValue"
    comment: >-
      The selected value equals this one, or is an array containing an element equal to it
      (strings are templates).
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:exists
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "exists"
    comment: >-
      When true, the pointer selects a value; when false, it selects nothing.
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:count
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "count"
    comment: >-
      The selected array has this many elements (an object, this many members).
    range: xsd:integer
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:jsonType
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "jsonType"
    comment: >-
      The selected value's JSON type: string, number, boolean, null, array or object.
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:capture
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "capture"
    comment: >-
      Binds a variable, for later steps, to the value this expectation located: a Link
      target (absolute), a header value, an auth-param value, the Location (absolute), or
      a JSON value. (A prerequisite resource binds its variable through container or
      dataResource.)
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:cleanup
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "cleanup"
    comment: >-
      When true, the captured Location is deleted, as the same identity, when the test
      ends.
    domain: lwst:LocationExpectation
    range: xsd:boolean
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:kind
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "kind"
    comment: >-
      The identity's kind.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: lwst:IdentityKind
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:suite
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "suite"
    comment: >-
      The authentication suite specification the credential follows.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdfs:Resource
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:tokenType
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "tokenType"
    comment: >-
      The RFC 8693 token type URI the credential is presented with.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdfs:Resource
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:algorithm
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "algorithm"
    comment: >-
      The signature algorithm the credential is signed with (a JOSE alg, or an XML-DSig
      algorithm URI for SAML).
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:webid
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "webid"
    comment: >-
      Template for the agent IRI of a harness-hosted identity; ${identity.<name>.webid}
      resolves to it.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:basis
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "basis"
    comment: >-
      The identity a fault identity is derived from.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: xsd:string
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:fault
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "fault"
    comment: >-
      The single defect of a fault identity.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: lwst:Fault
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:credentialHeader
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "credentialHeader"
    comment: >-
      Template for the JOSE header of a JWT credential.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:credentialClaims
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "credentialClaims"
    comment: >-
      Template for the claims set of a JWT credential.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:identityDocument
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "identityDocument"
    comment: >-
      Template for the controlled identifier document the harness serves at the identity's
      webid.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
  - id: lwst:samlAssertion
    type: rdf:Property
    label: "samlAssertion"
    comment: >-
      The fields of the SAML assertion the harness IdP issues for the identity.
    domain: lwst:Identity
    range: rdf:JSON
    isDefinedBy: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws-tests/v1
